# Vendored Triton AOT artifacts are generated code (embedded cubins): collapse
# in diffs/review and exclude from language stats. Regen: scripts/regen-triton-aot.sh
src/vt/cuda/triton_aot_vendored/** linguist-generated=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RULE: if a file's SHA256 is compared against a value recorded in a COMMITTED
# manifest, its bytes must not depend on the platform that checked it out.
#
# `file(SHA256 ...)` hashes the WORKING TREE. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf rewrites LF to CRLF, so an identical file hashes differently
# there -- and every one of these checks then fails on Windows alone while
# passing on Linux. `-text` tells git never to convert them in either
# direction, which is the accurate statement for content that IS the hash.
#
# MEASURED, cuda_windows, the only lane that both checks out on Windows and
# consumes these trees (the other Windows lanes build with CUDA off and never
# reach triton_aot_finalize):
#
#   TritonAOT.cmake:594  generator shim differs        <- the .py below
#   TritonAOT.cmake:636  artifact hash mismatch:       <- the vendored .c below
#                        gdn_chunko_bf16_h32...c
#
# The second was found the hard way: the first fix pinned ONLY the .py, and the
# very next lines of the same function hash .c and .h files. Fixing one instance
# of a class that is visible in the same function is not fixing the class.
#
# Hashed sources (TritonAOT.cmake:533,540,550,591,634,661;
# TritonAOTMultiArch.cmake:75,96,136):
scripts/triton-aot-compile.py -text
triton_kernels/*.py -text
src/vt/cuda/triton_aot_vendored/** -text

